Z||000000||Philphine||05-29-2001||12:49 PM||||<BR>i got one of bubbajoes mount kits, mainly because he said he may stop making them for a while during a hospital stay, and they seemed cheap enough to just get and have in case a caddy engine comes my way.<P>i have the 5speed izuzu in my '87 coupe but i also have access (i think) to one of the economy 4speeds from an '84. if i get going on something which might be better to use? would i give up much gas mileage wise switching to the four speed? is the 5speed as strong as the 4speed would be? would it complicate things computerwise (i have the 4speed shifter, cables and bracket)? thanks for any help. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||05-30-2001||09:35 AM||||say?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-30-2001||10:06 AM||||90% of economy is engine rpm when holding a steady speed on level ground.<P>  If you keep the engine down around 1500 rpm you will get the best mileage/gallon (up to about 55 or 60, if you are going 80mph and your engine is turning 1500 then you probally lugging it).<P>  which gear that turns out to be, at what speed, depends on the final gear ratio for that tranny/transaxel||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||05-30-2001||12:39 PM||||The unfortunate truth is that NONE of the transmissions available for the Fiero are geared that tall. (unless you want to go with 35" swampers)<P>1500 RPM is NOT lugging an engine.<BR>800 RPM is lugging an engine.<P>The 5 speed will definitely give you better gas mileage than the four speed.<BR>The reliability issue is probably a wash as long as you don't abuse it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-30-2001||01:21 PM||||Granted this is not a 4 speed tranny but at 4500 (75 mph) rpm the gas milage heads straight to the basement! I have found that anywhere in the yellow hached range the gas milage suffers GREATLY! compaired to 70 mph @ 4300 or there abouts rpm witch is the lower end of the yellow hached area.<P>    <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/carlisle/image002.jpg">    <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/sig.jpg">    <P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
